## Race Condition Guard

`needsContextRefresh` flag on Creature blocks ALL creature movement packets (except the player's own) during the transition window. Without this, movements queued before the switch get sent after, causing "creature not found" errors.

## Stackpos Calculation Order

When removing creatures from client during context switch, sort by **descending stackpos** within the same tile position. This ensures lower stackpos values stay valid after higher ones are removed.

## Known Issues (Not Yet Fixed)

- NPCs in context 0 are invisible in private contexts
- Stairs/holes/ladders don't work in private contexts (actionId/uniqueId not preserved)
- Movement breaks outside pre-loaded tile radius
- No monster respawn system for private contexts
- No context cleanup when all players leave

## Development Philosophy

- **Reuse existing game mechanics** — the game already has solutions (ghost, teleport, spectators). Read and reuse, don't reinvent.
- **Server-side filtering only** — the client doesn't need to know about contexts. All filtering happens on the server.
- **No client engine changes** — everything works with standard OT protocol packets.
- **Analyze before coding** — when stuck, study how the existing game handles the same problem (e.g., /ghost for visibility, sendMoveCreature for teleports).
